NAME
    stat - show a file's metadata

SYNOPSIS
    stat PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Print what the filesystem records about PATH: its type, its mode both
    symbolically and in octal, its owner (name, uid and gid), its size,
    its link count and its inode number.

    Through a session's capability the mode shown is the truth about who
    may do what, which is not always the bits stored on the disk; see
    fs.policy(5).

SEE ALSO
    chmod(1), chown(8), ls(1), ln(1)
